Session 5, 2026-09-05, Ag Leader InCommand 1200 (New Holland tractor).
Run 3 -- isolation test. IsobusVtInterface::Update()'s call to
updateVtVariables() was fully disabled (#if 0'd around it, reverted
immediately after this run -- see git history/HardwareTestNotes.md, not
left in the shipped code) to test whether our own post-connect
send_change_numeric_value() burst is what makes the VT stop sending its
status broadcast. Result: identical failure signature to run 2 -- exactly 4
status messages, then silence, then Status Timeout at almost exactly the
same elapsed time. This rules out our own outbound VT traffic as the cause.

Timestamps are seconds since the logging script attached to COM4; the
firmware flash that produced this run reset the board, so t=0 is close to
actual board reset this time.

